-- title:
--   Irreducibility of the projective Weierstrass cubic
-- statement:
--   Fix a commutative ring $F$ and a projective Weierstrass curve $V$ over $F$, i.e. data $a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4,a_6$ together with the homogeneous cubic $V.\mathtt{polynomial} = Y^2Z + a_1XYZ + a_3YZ^2 - X^3 - a_2X^2Z - a_4XZ^2 - a_6Z^3$ in three variables $X = X_0$, $Y = X_1$, $Z = X_2$. The module's one definition, `wCubic V`, is the cubic in one variable over $F[Y,Z]$ (a two-variable polynomial ring, with $X_0, X_1$ there playing the roles of $Y,Z$) whose coefficients are, in descending order, $1$, $a_2Z$, $a_4Z^2 - a_1YZ$ and $a_6Z^3 - Y^2Z - a_3YZ^2$. Three coefficient lemmas record these entries, and `finSuccEquiv_polynomial` states that the image of $V.\mathtt{polynomial}$ under the isomorphism $F[X_0,X_1,X_2] \cong (F[X_0,X_1])[X]$ splitting off the first variable is $-\,$`(wCubic V).toPoly`.
--
--   The remaining results exploit this presentation. `wCubic_toPoly_monic` and, over a domain, `wCubic_toPoly_natDegree` give monicity and degree $3$; `wCubic_isEisensteinAt` asserts the Eisenstein condition at the ideal generated by $Z$ (leading coefficient outside the ideal, lower coefficients inside it, constant coefficient outside its square), whence `irreducible_wCubic_toPoly` and, transporting along the isomorphism, `irreducible_polynomial`: the Weierstrass cubic is irreducible over any domain, hence nonzero and not a unit. When $F$ is moreover a unique factorisation domain, it is prime, the ideal it spans is prime, and the quotient $F[X,Y,Z]/(V.\mathtt{polynomial})$ is an integral domain. Independently of domain hypotheses, `isHomogeneous_polynomial` gives homogeneity of degree $3$, and over a domain the total degree is $3$. A final group of declarations instantiates all of this at the two rational curves $\langle 0,0,1,0,0\rangle$ and $\langle 0,0,0,1,0\rangle$, including the values $2$ and $1$ of their cubics at $(0,1,1)$ and the resulting distinctness of the two polynomials.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** Built entirely on Mathlib: `WeierstrassCurve.Projective` and its `polynomial`, Mathlib's `Cubic` type, `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt`, and the isomorphism `MvPolynomial.finSuccEquiv`. The only new notion is the auxiliary one-variable cubic `wCubic` over the coefficient ring $F[Y,Z]$.
--
--   **Where it is used.** The primality of the Weierstrass cubic, and the consequent integrality of the quotient ring, are what is needed to treat $F[X,Y,Z]/(V.\mathtt{polynomial})$ as the homogeneous coordinate ring of a projective Weierstrass model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_AlgebraicGeometry_ProjectiveWeierstrassPolynomialPrime.lean

